  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-04-07T14:34:11.206Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I am in deaf communities. Often I have noticed hearing (speaking) people join, and then try to learn sign language but end up using their voices to communicate. While it's difficult to understand if they keep getting frustrated and going back to use their voices, I would like to suggest this feature for the general public use so we can work together and get over the language barrier and help each other to learn how to sign and communicate with each other. It would be useful if it has the options to disable/enable if you don't need to use them or want to use them just in case somebody approaches a deaf person and try to talk to them verbally in public worlds. That'd be swell. Optional feature: subtitles appear over their heads and the words are facing at you so you can read them while they talk to you if that works.\n\nEDIT: Second Optional feature: If you're an RPG player and you prefer this, have the subtitles show up on your HUD instead of above their heads. it'll look like this;\nName1: *text*\nName2: *text*\n(April 7, 2021)\n\nSecond Edit: (10/21/2021)\nMade some edits on grammar errors and such.\nI also have an interesting suggestion; One day I found out the headset has a pointer-click (invisible computer mouse if you will) in the exact center of the HUD. That made me think of this new idea: Possible Optional, you look at the person, and the subtitles will focus on that person and transcribe what they are saying, ignoring the rest of the people around you (if you don't like the background chatter) so I think that'd be a neat idea.",
